387. drop temp_F_g_XX
388. 
. ///// If continuous option specified, generating polynomials of D_{g,1},
> ///// storing D_{g,1} somewhere, and replacing it by 0.
> if `continuous'>0{
389.         
.         scalar degree_pol = `continuous'
390.         
. forvalues pol_level = 1/`=degree_pol'{
391.         scalar pol_level_XX = `pol_level'
392.         capture drop d_sq_`pol_level'_XX 
393.         gen d_sq_`pol_level'_XX = d_sq_XX^scalar(pol_level_XX)
394. }
395. capture drop d_sq_XX_orig
396. gen d_sq_XX_orig=d_sq_XX
397. replace d_sq_XX=0
398. }
399. 
. // Create a new variable = to d_sq_XX expressed in integers
. capture drop d_sq_int_XX
400. 
. gegen d_sq_int_XX = group(d_sq_XX)
401. 
. ///// Dropping the values of the baseline treatment such that no variance in F_g within those values.
> capture drop var_F_g_XX
402. bys d_sq_XX `trends_nonparam': gegen var_F_g_XX=sd(F_g_XX)
403. drop if var_F_g_XX==0
404. drop var_F_g_XX
405. 
. //// CHANGE BELOW - tks
> //// Counting number of groups after the drop above
> cap drop group2_XX
406. egen group2_XX = group(group_XX)
407. sum group2_XX
408. scalar G_XX=r(max)
409. ////
> 
. ///// Error message if Design Restriction 1 is not met.
> count
410. if r(N)==0{
411.         di as error ""
412.         di as error "No treatment effect can be estimated. This is because Design Restriction 1 in de
>  Chaisemartin & D'Haultfoeuille (2024) is not satisfied in the data, given the options requested. This m
> ay be due to the fact that groups' period-one treatment is continuous, or takes a large number of values
> , and you have not specified the continuous option. If so, you can try to specify this option. If the is
> sue persists even with this option, this means that all groups experience their first treatment change a
> t the same date, a situation where the estimators of de Chaisemartin & D'Haultfoeuille (2024) cannot be 
> used."
413.         di as input _continue ""
414. 
.         exit
415. }
416. 
. ///// For each value of the baseline treatment, we drop time periods such that we do not have any contro
> l with that baseline treatment after that period
> ///// This means the panel is no longer balanced, though it is balanced within values of the baseline tr
> eatment
> gen never_change_d_XX=1-ever_change_d_XX
417. bys time_XX d_sq_XX `trends_nonparam': gegen controls_time_XX=max(never_change_d_XX)
418. drop if controls_time_XX==0
419. 
. ///// Computing t_min_XX, T_max_XX, and replacing F_g_XX by last period plus one for those that never ch
> ange treatment
> sum time_XX
420. scalar t_min_XX=r(min)
421. scalar T_max_XX=r(max)
422. replace F_g_XX=T_max_XX+1 if F_g_XX==0
423. 
. ///// Dealing with missing treatments: most conservative option
> 
. *Let FMD_g denote the first date when g's treatment is missing while y has been not missing at least onc
> e, so that we know for sure that g already exists. If that date is before the first period when g's trea
> tment changes, we do not know when g's treatment has changed for the first time. Then, a conservative op
> tion is to drop all of g's outcomes starting at FMD_g.
. 
. if "`drop_if_d_miss_before_first_switch'"!=""{
424. replace outcome_XX=. if min_time_d_miss_aft_ynm_XX<F_g_XX&time_XX>=min_time_d_miss_aft_ynm_XX
425. }
426. 
. ///// Dealing with missing treatments: most liberal option
> 
. *Let FD_g and LD_g respectively denote the first and last period where a group's treatment is non missin
> g. Let FY_g denote the first period where a group's outcome is non missing.
. 
. *For groups that experience at least one treatment change, let LDBF_g denote the last date before F_g wh
> ere g's treatment is non missing. We have FD_g<=LDBF_g<F_g<=LD_g, and we will deal with missing treatmen
> ts depending on when they occur with respect to those four dates.
. 
. capture drop last_obs_D_bef_switch_t_XX
427. capture drop last_obs_D_bef_switch_XX
428. gen last_obs_D_bef_switch_t_XX=time_XX if time_XX<F_g_XX&treatment_XX!=.
429. bys group_XX: gegen last_obs_D_bef_switch_XX=max(last_obs_D_bef_switch_t_XX)
430. 
. *For groups that do not experience a treatment change, we just have FD_g<=LD_g, and we will deal with mi
> ssing treatments depending on when they occur with respect to those two dates.
. 
. *For t<FD_g, by default we are going to consider that g joins the panel at FD_g: any non-missing outcome
>  before FD_g replaced as missing, but all non-missing outcomes after FD_g are kept. For groups such that
>  FY_g<FD_g, this is a "liberal" convention: those groups exist before FD_g, so one could argue that thei
> r status quo treatment is missing and they should be dropped from the analysis. We give the user the opt
> ion to do that, with drop_if_d_miss_before_first_switch option
.   
. replace outcome_XX=. if time_XX<min_time_d_nonmiss_XX 
431. 
. *For groups that experience a treatment change, if D_gt missing at FD_g<t<LDBF_g, we replace their missi
> ng treatment by their status-quo treatment. Again, this is a liberal convention, so we give the user the
>  option to not use those observations, with drop_if_d_miss_before_first_switch option.
. 
. replace treatment_XX=d_sq_XX if F_g_XX<T_max_XX+1&treatment_XX==.&time_XX<last_obs_D_bef_switch_XX&time_
> XX>min_time_d_nonmiss_XX
432. 
. *For groups that experience a treatment change, if D_gt missing at LDBF_g<t<F_g (equivalent to LDBF_g<F_
> g-1), we cannot know the exact date when their treatment has changed, even in a binary and staggered des
> ign. Therefore, we set their outcomes at missing starting at LDBF_g+1. We also redefine their F_g as T+1
>  because they are effectively control groups. We also define the trunc_control_XX as LDBF_g+1 for them, 
> because they can only be used as controls till that date.
. 
. replace outcome_XX=. if F_g_XX<T_max_XX+1&time_XX>last_obs_D_bef_switch_XX&last_obs_D_bef_switch_XX<F_g_
> XX-1
433. capture drop trunc_control_XX
434. gen trunc_control_XX=last_obs_D_bef_switch_XX+1 if F_g_XX<T_max_XX+1&last_obs_D_bef_switch_XX<F_g_XX-
> 1
435. replace F_g_XX=T_max_XX+1 if F_g_XX<T_max_XX+1&last_obs_D_bef_switch_XX<F_g_XX-1
436. 
. *For groups that experience a treatment change, if D_gt missing at F_g<t, we replace their missing treat
> ment by D(g,F_g). This is again a liberal convention, but it is innocuous for the reduced-form parameter
> s DID_l, so we do not give the user the option to overrule it (Note that overruling it could make the sa
> me_switchers option fail)
. 
. gen d_F_g_temp_XX = treatment_XX if time_XX==F_g_XX
437. bys group_XX: gegen d_F_g_XX = mean(d_F_g_temp_XX)
438. replace treatment_XX=d_F_g_XX if F_g_XX<T_max_XX+1&treatment_XX==.&time_XX>F_g_XX&last_obs_D_bef_swit
> ch_XX==F_g_XX-1
439. 
. *For groups that do not experience a treatment change, if D_gt missing at FD_g<t<LD_g, we replace their 
> missing treatment by D_g1. This is again a liberal convention, so we give the user the option to not use
>  those observations, with drop_if_d_miss_before_first_switch option.
. 
. replace treatment_XX=d_sq_XX if F_g_XX==T_max_XX+1&treatment_XX==.&time_XX>min_time_d_nonmiss_XX&time_XX
> <max_time_d_nonmiss_XX
440. 
. *For groups that do not experience a treatment change, we replace all their outcomes by missing at t>LD_
> g. Even in a binary and staggered design, we cannot infer their treatment at t>LD_g.
. 
. replace outcome_XX=. if F_g_XX==T_max_XX+1&time_XX>max_time_d_nonmiss_XX
441. replace trunc_control_XX=max_time_d_nonmiss_XX+1 if F_g_XX==T_max_XX+1
442. 
. ///// Store the outcome in levels, will be useful later when predict_het and trends_lin specified
> if "`predict_het_good'"!=""{
443. gen outcome_non_diff_XX=outcome_XX
444. }
445. 
. ///// If trends_lin option specified, drop units for which F_g_XX==2, and redefine 
> ///// outcome and controls in first difference.
> if "`trends_lin'"!=""{
446.         drop if F_g_XX==2
447.         xtset group_XX time_XX
448.         capture drop FD_outcome_XX
449.         gen FD_outcome_XX =outcome_XX-L.outcome_XX
450.         replace outcome_XX = FD_outcome_XX
451.         drop FD_outcome_XX
452.         
.         // adapt controls for case where trends_lin by and continuous specified together
.         if "`trends_lin'"!=""&"`by'"!=""&`continuous'!=0{
453.         local controls = "`controls_orig_XX'"
454. }
455.         
.         if "`controls'" !=""{
456.         foreach var of varlist `controls'{
457.         capture drop FD_`var'_XX
458.         gen FD_`var'_XX =`var' -L.`var'
459.         replace `var' = FD_`var'_XX
460.         drop FD_`var'_XX
461.         }
462.         }
463.         drop if time_XX==1
464.         sum time_XX
465.         scalar t_min_XX=r(min)
466. }
467. 
. ///// Balancing the panel
> cap rename _merge _merge_og
468. fillin group_XX time_XX
469. capture drop d_sq_XX_new
470. bys group_XX: gegen d_sq_XX_new=mean(d_sq_XX)
471. drop d_sq_XX
472. rename d_sq_XX_new d_sq_XX
473. 
. ///// CHANGE BELOW - tks
> 
. bys group_XX: gegen d_sq_int_XX_new = mean(d_sq_int_XX)
474. drop d_sq_int_XX
475. rename d_sq_int_XX_new d_sq_int_XX
476. 
. bys group_XX: gegen F_g_XX_new = mean(F_g_XX)
477. drop F_g_XX
478. rename F_g_XX_new F_g_XX
479. 
. /////
> 
. ///// Defining N_gt, the weight of each cell (g,t)
> gen N_gt_XX=1
480. replace N_gt_XX = N_gt_XX*weight_XX  //
481. replace N_gt_XX=0 if outcome_XX==.|treatment_XX==.
482. 
. ///// Determining last period where g still has a control group:
> ///// There is still a group with same 
> ///// treatment as g's in period 1 and whose treatment has not changed since 
> ///// start of panel. Definition adapted from the paper, to account for 
> ///// imbalanced panel.
> 
. capture drop F_g_trunc_XX
483. gen F_g_trunc_XX=F_g_XX
484. replace F_g_trunc_XX=min(F_g_XX,trunc_control_XX) if trunc_control_XX!=.
485. bys d_sq_XX `trends_nonparam': gegen T_g_XX = max(F_g_trunc_XX) 
486. replace T_g_XX = T_g_XX-1
487. 
. ///// Defining S_g: 
> ///// an indicator variable for groups whose average post switch 
> ///// treatment value is larger than their initial treatment D_{g,1}. 
> ///// They will be considered switchers in. If S_g==0, the group is a switcher out. 
> ///// For never-switchers, S_g is undefined.
> ///// Definition of S_g matches that in paper, unless dont_drop_larger_lower specified.
> 
. bys group_XX : gegen avg_post_switch_treat_XX_temp = total(treatment_XX) if time_XX>=F_g_XX&time_XX<=T_g
> _XX
488. gen count_time_post_switch_XX_temp=(treatment_XX!=.) if time_XX>=F_g_XX&time_XX<=T_g_XX
489. bysort group_XX : gegen count_time_post_switch_XX=total(count_time_post_switch_XX_temp)
490. replace avg_post_switch_treat_XX_temp =avg_post_switch_treat_XX_temp/count_time_post_switch_XX
491. bys group_XX: gegen avg_post_switch_treat_XX=mean(avg_post_switch_treat_XX_temp)
492. drop avg_post_switch_treat_XX_temp
493. 
. // When a group is a switching group, but its average post-treatment treatment 
. // value is exactly equal to its baseline treatment, we cannnot classify it as 
. // a swicher in or a switcher out, but it is not a control either. 
. // As such, we drop it from the estimation. Those groups are referred to 
. // as no-first-stage-switchers. This issue can only arise 
. // if dont_drop_larger_lower specified. 
. // if continuous is specified we do this according to the original 
. // baseline treatment and not to the one set to 0 to correctly
. // track if a group is switcher in or switcher out.
. if `continuous'==0{
494.         drop if avg_post_switch_treat_XX==d_sq_XX&F_g_XX!=T_g_XX+1
495.         gen S_g_XX=(avg_post_switch_treat_XX>d_sq_XX) if F_g_XX!=T_max_XX+1
496. }
497. else if `continuous'>0{
498.         drop if avg_post_switch_treat_XX==d_sq_XX_orig&F_g_XX!=T_g_XX+1
499.         gen S_g_XX=(avg_post_switch_treat_XX>d_sq_XX_orig) if F_g_XX!=T_max_XX+1
500. }       
501. // correct for the fact that if all avg_post_switch_treat_XX are missing it is considered as +inf
. egen aux_XX = min(avg_post_switch_treat_XX), by(group_XX)
502. replace S_g_XX = . if aux_XX ==.
503. 
. // Define another version where S_g=-1 for switchers out, which we need 
. // when predict_het or continuous specified.
. if "`predict_het_good'"!="" | `continuous'>0{
504. gen S_g_het_XX=S_g_XX
505. replace S_g_het_XX=-1 if S_g_het_XX==0
506. if "`predict_het_good'"!=""{
507. scalar heterogeneity_scalar_XX=1
508. }
509. }
510. 
. 
. ///// If continuous option specified: binarizing and staggerizing treatment,
> ///// and adding time_FEs interacted with D_{g,1} as controls
> if `continuous'>0{
511. 
. //Binarizing and staggerizing treatment
. capture drop treatment_XX_temp
512. gen treatment_XX_temp = (F_g_XX<=time_XX)*S_g_het_XX if S_g_het_XX!=.
513. capture drop treatment_XX_orig
514. gen treatment_XX_orig=treatment_XX
515. replace treatment_XX = treatment_XX_temp 
516. 
. //Enriching controls
. tab time_XX, gen(time_fe_XX_)
517. local max_time_XX=r(r)
518. // Modif Clément: actually, to compute the estimator with the continuous option we need to control fo
> r polynomial in D_{g,1} interacted with \sum_{k=1}^t'1\{t=k}, sum of period FEs up to t'.
. forvalue i=2/`max_time_XX'{
519. replace time_fe_XX_`i'=(time_XX>=`i')
520. }
521. // End modif Clément
. foreach var of varlist time_fe_XX_2-time_fe_XX_`max_time_XX'{
522.         forvalues pol_level = 1/`=degree_pol'{
523.                 gen `var'_bt`pol_level'_XX = `var'*d_sq_`pol_level'_XX
524.                 local controls "`controls' `var'_bt`pol_level'_XX"
525.         }
526.         capture drop `var'
527. }
528. capture drop time_fe_XX_1
529. }
530. 
. ///// Creating treatment at F_g: D_{g,F_g}
> gen d_fg_XX_temp=treatment_XX if time_XX==F_g_XX
531. bys group_XX: gegen d_fg_XX=mean(d_fg_XX_temp)
532. replace d_fg_XX=d_sq_XX if d_fg_XX==. & F_g_XX==T_max_XX+1
533. drop d_fg_XX_temp 
534. 
. ///// Creating the variable L_g_XX = T_g_XX - F_g_XX, so that we can compute L_u or L_a afterwards.
> gen L_g_XX = T_g_XX - F_g_XX +1
535. 
. ///// Creating the equivalent variable L_g_placebo_XX for the placebos.
> if `placebo'!=0{
536. capture drop L_g_placebo_XX
537. gen L_g_placebo_XX = min(L_g_XX, F_g_XX-2) if F_g_XX>=3
538. }
539. 
. ///// Tagging first observation of each group_XX.
> sort group_XX time_XX
540. bysort group_XX : gen first_obs_by_gp_XX = (_n==1)
541. 
. ///// If cluster option specified, tagging first observation of each cluster, 
> ///// and checking clustering variable weakly coarser than group variable.
> 
. if "`cluster'"!=""{
542.                 
.         // FELIX 06-03-25 -> I guess this is how Tom solved it 
.         cap drop cluster_group_XX
543.         bysort group_XX: gegen cluster_group_XX=min(`cluster') 
544.         bysort group_XX: replace `cluster'=cluster_group_XX if `cluster'==.
545.         // Can do this because clusters have to be coarser than groups
.         
.         capture drop cluster_var_g_XX
546.         
.         bysort `cluster' (group_XX time_XX) : gen first_obs_by_clust_XX = (_n==1) if `cluster'!=. // FEL
> IX 05_03_25 -> This is then not needed anymore
547.         
.         //Error message for clustering: non-nested case
.         bysort group_XX: gegen cluster_var_g_XX = sd(`cluster')
548.         sum cluster_var_g_XX
549.         scalar max_cluster_var_XX = `r(max)'
550.         if (scalar(max_cluster_var_XX) >0){
551.         di as error ""
552.         di as error "The group variable should be nested within the clustering variable."
553.         di as input _continue ""
554.         exit
555.         }
556.         
. }
557. 
. ///// Declaring data as panel //
> xtset group_XX time_XX
558. 
. ///// Creating first-differenced outcome and treatment//
> capture drop diff_y_XX
559. capture drop diff_d_XX
560. gen diff_y_XX = d.outcome_XX
561. g diff_d_XX = d.treatment_XX
562. 
. ////////// 3. Necessary pre-estimation steps when the controls option is specified.     
> 
. if "`controls'" !=""{
563. local count_controls=0
564. 
. capture drop fd_X_all_non_missing_XX
565. gen fd_X_all_non_missing_XX=1
566. 
. foreach var of varlist `controls'{
567. 
. local count_controls=`count_controls'+1
568. 
. capture drop diff_X`count_controls'_XX
569. capture drop avg_diff_X`count_controls'_XX
570. capture drop resid_X`count_controls'_time_FE_XX
571. 
. ///// Computing the first differences of the control variables
> 
. xtset group_XX time_XX
572. gen diff_X`count_controls'_XX=D.`var'
573. replace fd_X_all_non_missing_XX=0 if diff_X`count_controls'_XX==.
574. }
575. 
. ///// Residualization, and computation of term entering variance. 
> 
. local count_controls=0
576. local mycontrols_XX ""
577. local prod_controls_y ""
578. 
. foreach var of varlist `controls'{
579. local count_controls=`count_controls'+1
580. 
. capture drop sum_weights_control_XX //So as to consider the weighted regressions.
581. 
. // Computing  \Delta X_{.,t}: average of controls' first difference at time t, 
. // among groups whose treatment has not changed yet.
. 
. bys time_XX d_sq_XX `trends_nonparam' : gegen sum_weights_control_XX = total(N_gt_XX) if ever_change_d_X
> X==0&diff_y_XX!=.&fd_X_all_non_missing_XX==1
582. bys time_XX d_sq_XX `trends_nonparam' : gegen avg_diff_X`count_controls'_XX = total(N_gt_XX*diff_X`co
> unt_controls'_XX) if ever_change_d_XX==0&diff_y_XX!=.&fd_X_all_non_missing_XX==1
583. 
. bys time_XX d_sq_XX `trends_nonparam' : replace avg_diff_X`count_controls'_XX = avg_diff_X`count_control
> s'_XX/sum_weights_control_XX
584. 
. // Computing \Delta\Dot{X}_{g,t}, the difference between the first differences 
. // of covariates and the average of their first-difference, which gives us 
. // the residuals of a regression of covariates on time fixed effects. 
. //Multiply by sqrt(N_gt_XX) to replicate weighted regression.
. 
. gen resid_X`count_controls'_time_FE_XX = sqrt(N_gt_XX)*(diff_X`count_controls'_XX - avg_diff_X`count_con
> trols'_XX)
585. 
. replace resid_X`count_controls'_time_FE_XX=0 if resid_X`count_controls'_time_FE_XX==.
586. 
. // Storing the obtained residuals for the computation of theta_d
. local mycontrols_XX "`mycontrols_XX' resid_X`count_controls'_time_FE_XX"
587. 
. // Generating the product between \Delta\Dot{X}_{g,t} and \Delta Y_{g,t}
. //Multiply by sqrt(N_gt_XX) to replicate weighted regression
. capture drop prod_X`count_controls'_Ngt_XX
588. // Delete those we do not need anymore
. capture drop prod_X`count_controls'_diff_y_temp_XX
589. capture drop prod_X`count_controls'_diff_y_XX
590. capture drop diff_y_wXX
591. gen diff_y_wXX = sqrt(N_gt_XX)*diff_y_XX
592. 
. * Note: resid_X`count_controls'_time_FE_XX is already multiplied by sqrt(N_gt_XX)
. gen prod_X`count_controls'_Ngt_XX=resid_X`count_controls'_time_FE_XX*sqrt(N_gt_XX)
593. replace prod_X`count_controls'_Ngt_XX=0 if prod_X`count_controls'_Ngt_XX==. 
594. 
. }
595. 
. ///// Computing the Den_d matrices and their inverts,
> ///// and creating locals storing the status quos for which Den_d^{-1} not defined. 
> 
. local store_singular_XX ""
596. local store_noresidualization_XX ""
597. local levels_d_sq_XX_final ""
598. 
. levelsof d_sq_int_XX, local(levels_d_sq_XX)
599. 
. foreach l of local levels_d_sq_XX {
600.         
. capture drop E_y_hat_gt_int_`l'_XX              
601. 
. // Running residualization regression to compute predicted values
. 
. local controlsXX ""
602. forv i = 1/`count_controls'{
603.         local controlsXX "`controlsXX' diff_X`i'_XX"
604. }
605. 
. *Modif Clément 30/6/2025
. *cap reg diff_y_XX `controlsXX' ibn.time_XX [aw=N_gt_XX] if d_sq_int_XX==`l'&time_XX<F_g_XX, noconst
. if "`trends_nonparam'" == "" {
606. cap reg diff_y_XX `controlsXX' ibn.time_XX [aw=N_gt_XX] if d_sq_int_XX==`l'&time_XX<F_g_XX, noconst
607. }
608. if "`trends_nonparam'" != "" {
609. capture drop trends_nonparam_temp_XX
610. gegen trends_nonparam_temp_XX=group(`trends_nonparam')  
611. cap reg diff_y_XX `controlsXX' ibn.time_XX#ibn.trends_nonparam_temp_XX [aw=N_gt_XX] if d_sq_int_XX==`
> l'&time_XX<F_g_XX, noconst
612. }
613. *End Modif Clément 19/6/2025
. 
. if (_rc == 0) {
614. predict E_y_hat_gt_int_`l'_XX if d_sq_int_XX==`l'&time_XX<F_g_XX
615. *Modif Clément 19/6/2025
. capture drop trends_nonparam_temp_XX
616. *End Modif Clément 19/6/2025
.         tempfile data_XX
617.         save "`data_XX'.dta", replace
618.         
. // A baseline treatment is relevant iff it is taken by at least two groups with different values of F_g_
> XX
. // and non-missing diff_y_XX, otherwise we do not need to perform the residualization for this specific 
> baseline treatment.
. 
. scalar store_singular_`l'_XX = 0 
619. tab F_g_XX if d_sq_int_XX==`l'  
620. 
. scalar useful_res_`l'_XX = `r(r)'
621.         if (scalar(useful_res_`l'_XX)>1){
622. 
. // Isolate the observations used in the computation of theta_d
. 
. keep if ever_change_d_XX==0&diff_y_XX!=.&fd_X_all_non_missing_XX==1&d_sq_int_XX==`l'
623. 
. // Using the matrix accum function, to regress the first difference of outcome on the first differences 
> of covariates. We will obtain the vectors of coefficients \theta_d s, where d indexes values of the base
> line treatment.
. 
. capture matrix accum overall_XX = diff_y_wXX `mycontrols_XX'
624. scalar rc_XX=_rc
625. 
. if scalar(rc_XX)!=0{
626. scalar store_singular_`l'_XX = 1
627. local store_noresidualization_XX "`store_noresidualization_XX' `l'"
628. scalar useful_res_`l'_XX=1
629. }
630. 
. else {
631.         
. // Isolate the parts of the matrix we need
. matrix didmgt_XX = overall_XX[2..`=`count_controls'+1',2..`=`count_controls'+1']
632. matrix didmgt_Xy = overall_XX[2..`=`count_controls'+1',1]
633. 
. // Computing the vectors of coefficients \theta_d s for each value of the baseline treatment
. matrix coefs_sq_`l'_XX = invsym(didmgt_XX)*didmgt_Xy
634. local levels_d_sq_XX_final "`levels_d_sq_XX_final' `l'" // Added local so as to avoid adding to the f
> inal block non-existent coefficients.
635. 
.                 // Computing the matrix Den^{-1}_d
.                         //Check first if the matrix is invertible, invsym() inverts a matrix even if it 
> is singular
.                         capture drop scalar det_XX
636.                         scalar det_XX = det(didmgt_XX)
637. 
.                 if (abs(scalar(det_XX))<=10^(-16)){ 
638.                                         scalar store_singular_`l'_XX = 1
639.                                         scalar drop det_XX
640.                 }
641. 
.                 // Changes Diego 27-03-25: N_c_`l'_XX adjustment
.                 sum F_g_XX
642.                 gen N_c_`l'_temp_XX = time_XX >= 2 & time_XX <= r(max) - 1 & time_XX < F_g_XX & diff_
> y_XX < .
643.                 sum N_gt_XX if N_c_`l'_temp_XX == 1
644. 
.                 matrix inv_Denom_`l'_XX = invsym(didmgt_XX)*r(sum)*G_XX
645.                 drop N_c_`l'_temp_XX
646. }
647. 
. use "`data_XX'.dta", clear
648. 
. }
649. }
650. else {
651. *Modif Clément 19/6/2025
. capture drop trends_nonparam_temp_XX
652. *End Modif Clément 19/6/2025   
.     drop if d_sq_int_XX == `l'
653.     noi di "Baseline Treatment Level `l' dropped because of insufficient observations."
654. }
655. 
. }
656. 
. //Fill up store_singular_XX, with correct values of statu quo and not the levels -> Modif Felix
. levelsof d_sq_XX, local(levels_d_sq_bis_XX)
657. scalar index_sing_XX = 0
658. foreach l of local levels_d_sq_bis_XX {
659.         scalar index_sing_XX = scalar(index_sing_XX)+1
660.         capture confirm scalar store_singular_`=index_sing_XX'_XX
661.         if _rc==0{
662.                 if(scalar(store_singular_`=index_sing_XX'_XX) == 1){
663.                 local store_singular_XX = "`store_singular_XX' `l'"
664.                 }
665.         }
666. }
667. 
. ///// Display errors if one of the Den_d^{-1} is not defined
> if ("`store_singular_XX'"!=""){
668.         
.         di as error "Some control variables are not taken into account for groups with baseline treatmen
> t equal to: [`store_singular_XX']"
669.         di as error "This may occur in the following situations:"
670.         di as error "1. For groups with those values of the baseline treatment, the regression of the
>  outcome first difference on the controls' first differences and time fixed effects has fewer observatio
> ns than variables. Note that for each value of the baseline treatment, those regressions are estimated a
> mong (g,t)s such that g has not changed treatment yet at t."
671.         di as error "2. For groups with those values of the baseline treatment, two or more of your c
> ontrol variables are perfectly collinear in the sample where the regression is run, for instance because
>  those control variables do not vary over time."
672.         di as input _continue ""
673. }
674. 
. ///// Values of baseline treatment such that residualization could not be performed at all are dropped.
> foreach l of local store_noresidualization_XX {
675. drop if d_sq_int_XX==`l'
676. }
677. 
. } // end of the if "`controls'" !="" condition
678. 
. ////////// 4. Performing the estimation and storing the results
> 
. ///// Computing L_u/L_a, maximum number of event-study effects that can be computed
> ///// for the switchers in/out, to compare them to number of effects requested,
> ///// and finally determine the number of effects to be estimated.
> ///// Same thing for the placebos.
> 
. // Initializing L_u_XX and L_a_XX with default values.
. scalar L_u_XX=.
679. scalar L_a_XX=.
680. 
. // For switchers in
. if "`switchers'"==""|"`switchers'"=="in"{ 
681. sum L_g_XX if S_g_XX==1
682. scalar L_u_XX=r(max)
683. *For placebos
. if `placebo'!=0{
684. sum L_g_placebo_XX if S_g_XX==1
685. scalar L_placebo_u_XX=r(max)
686. 
. // If the trends_lin option was specified, L_placebo_u_XX should be decreased by 1
. // because data starts at period 2 instead of 1.
. if "`trends_lin'"!=""{
687.         scalar L_placebo_u_XX=L_placebo_u_XX-1
688. }
689. if L_placebo_u_XX==. {
690.     scalar L_placebo_u_XX = 0
691. }
692. }
693. }
694. 
. // For switchers out
. if "`switchers'"==""|"`switchers'"=="out"{
695. sum L_g_XX if S_g_XX==0
696. scalar L_a_XX=r(max)
697. *For placebos
